WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.560
A mouse tumor is grafted into a three-day-old chick embryo.

2
00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:11.060
The embryo's own nerve fibers invade it.

3
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:17.140
Sympathetic ganglia grow to about six times the size of the same ganglia in control

4
00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:23.160
embryos. A ganglion is a cluster of nerve cells outside the brain and spinal cord.

5
00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.020
Why do they swell?

6
00:00:25.683 --> 00:00:29.183
Start with the simplest explanation, contact.

7
00:00:30.023 --> 00:00:33.803
The tumor sits inside the embryo, pressed against its tissues.

8
00:00:35.063 --> 00:00:40.263
Bueker read his own result as the tumor offering a favorable field for fibers to

9
00:00:40.263 --> 00:00:42.983
grow into. So ask one question.

10
00:00:44.003 --> 00:00:46.223
Does the tumor need to touch the embryo?

11
00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:51.713
So Levi-Montalcini and Hamburger moved the tumor out.

12
00:00:52.573 --> 00:00:57.813
The chorioallantoic membrane is a thin sheet that lines the inside of the eggshell.

13
00:00:58.453 --> 00:01:01.093
It is plumbed into the embryo's blood circulation.

14
00:01:01.653 --> 00:01:04.473
It touches none of the embryo's internal tissue.

15
00:01:05.233 --> 00:01:06.993
They grafted the tumor there.

16
00:01:07.717 --> 00:01:12.117
The ganglia deep inside the embryo swelled just as before.

17
00:01:12.937 --> 00:01:15.037
Only blood connected the two tissues.

18
00:01:15.817 --> 00:01:19.397
So the tumor had to be putting something soluble into it.

19
00:01:20.097 --> 00:01:21.277
Contact is ruled out.

20
00:01:21.837 --> 00:01:24.097
A substance that travels is ruled in.

21
00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:29.457
The graft showed that a molecule must exist, but not what it was.
